Turn Wayle's audio dropdown into a Bluetooth and audio panel opened from
Waybar's audio button, with the tabs the Rofi menu it replaces used.

Pair hosts Wayle's own Bluetooth dropdown, so the Bluetooth component's root
becomes a box and its factory supplies the standalone popover. Output and
Input keep the native default-device row and device picker, and the picker
now expands a device whose profile exposes several plugged-in ports into one
row per port, activating the port before it makes the device default. Play is
the native per-application volume list plus a route button, which opens the
same device list in a mode that moves one playback stream instead.

The panel is registered for the external layer-shell window path and anchors
to the bar's trailing edge, where the Waybar audio button lives.

